      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__channel__getters_1ga7de70ef6bcadc6dd9f70d4f44511e130" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>const int</type>
        <definition>const int ndxlGetChannelEdges</definition>
        <argsstring>(NDXLChannel *_Channel, NDXLEdge **_Edges)</argsstring>
        <name>ndxlGetChannelEdges</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1a40b73c1a687ab1376515b42d4294c079" kindref="member">NDXLChannel</ref> *</type>
          <declname>_Channel</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1aa30ac2f40da4dbe7d841088a78f957fe" kindref="member">NDXLEdge</ref> **</type>
          <declname>_Edges</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Gets a list of all the edges affected by a noise channel. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Channel</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Target noise channel to retrieve the affected edges of.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="out">_Edges</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to a user-allocated array of <ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1aa30ac2f40da4dbe7d841088a78f957fe" kindref="member">NDXLEdge</ref> pointers. The array must contain at least ndxlGetChannelEdgeCount(_Channel) elements. The function populates the array in-place.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>If either _Channel or _Edges are NULL, returns <ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gae9261a8e1c9a6cebdc947ee5798cca1e" kindref="member">NDXL_ERR</ref>, otherwise populates _Edges with the edge pointers affected by _Channel, and returns NDXL_OK.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>The caller retains ownership of the array, but not of the <ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1aa30ac2f40da4dbe7d841088a78f957fe" kindref="member">NDXLEdge</ref> objects referenced by its elements. These pointers refer to the original objects in the network, so modifications through them affect those objects directly. The returned list can be used to modify or destroy its referenced objects without invalidating the array itself.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>The function does not verify the capacity of the supplied array. Providing an inadequately sized array can result in out-of-bounds writes and undefined behaviour.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Errors raised</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gaf6b8bdcb87bdd7944810152b510101e4" kindref="member">NDXL_ARG_ERR</ref> : _Channel is NULL.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gaf6b8bdcb87bdd7944810152b510101e4" kindref="member">NDXL_ARG_ERR</ref> : _Edges is NULL.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="group__channel__getters_1gae2a14deb284d756f55511e25fb57d48c" kindref="member">ndxlGetChannelEdgeCount</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
